# GTFS-RT Poller — Design Rules

## Endpoints (poll all concurrently every 15 s)

| Redis key | TfNSW path |
|-----------|------------|
| `gtfsrt:buses` | `/v1/gtfs/realtime/buses` |
| `gtfsrt:cbdlightrail` | `/v1/gtfs/realtime/lightrail/cbdandsoutheast` |
| `gtfsrt:sydneytrains` | `/v2/gtfs/realtime/sydneytrains` |
| `gtfsrt:metro` | `/v2/gtfs/realtime/metro` |
| `gtfsrt:innerwestlightrail` | `/v2/gtfs/realtime/lightrail/innerwest` |

## Concurrency (required)

- **`sync.WaitGroup` fan-out** per tick — never fetch endpoints sequentially
- Poll immediately on startup, then `time.Ticker`
- Per-round deadline: **80% of interval** (12 s @ 15 s)
- Shared `http.Client`, timeout **10 s**, `MaxIdleConnsPerHost = len(endpoints)`

## Download safety (required)

- Header: `Authorization: apikey <TFNSW_API_KEY>`
- Manual gzip + `io.LimitReader` at **32 MiB decompressed**
- Read `maxBodyBytes+1` to detect truncation
- Non-2xx or corrupt proto: **error, do not overwrite Redis**

## Redis (required)

- Store **raw protobuf bytes** — not JSON
- `proto.Unmarshal` to validate before `SET`
- TTL **30 s** (2 × poll interval)
- Pool size: `len(endpoints) + 2`

## When extending

- Add endpoints to `rtEndpoints` slice with distinct `gtfsrt:*` keys
- Keep `downloadFeed` and `fetchAndPublish` separation
- Gate `logFeedSample` behind debug flag in production (future)
